# EAS Build's own file-collector doesn't reliably support the root .gitignore's
# allowlist pattern (/* then !/frontend/ to re-include) the way real git does —
# some ignore-parsers drop a directory entirely once a parent pattern matches it,
# even if a later negation targets that exact directory. This file uses plain
# deny-list rules instead, so frontend/ (and agent/) are never at risk of being
# excluded by a misinterpreted negation.

.claude/
.pytest_cache/
docs/
run.py
tether-app-plan.md

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
